gaps.what:
Some fix side effects were noted with no verdict, and none of them is in a package or on Game-boy's list:
- the stomp: with stomp_stop_distance 0.45 the player's standing feet sit inside a lying body's pelvis and thighs, and the stomp foot's return passes through them (flash-and-looks fixer, 'remaining');
- side view: the stomp's low bar crosses the player's shins (ko-respawn-bars fixer);
- side-view piles: a lying body's bar crosses the standing body in front of it (hit reviewer, a result of the ragdoll-03 fix);
- the knee-KO body stands nearly upright for a few frames (launch-from-hold fixer).

Code notes that nobody has ruled on:
- blink_shown() hard-codes a 50% on/off duty (combat_actor.gd:260);
- _respawn_spot() hard-codes rings [1, 2] times 2 body radii (training_dummy.gd:290-294);
- return_home uses 60 frames and 0.3 m (pre-existing);
- humanoid_rig.gd:405 says a 3 m radius whites the whole body, while TuningData and ARCHITECTURE say about 4 m;
- stale comments: vfx_bot.gd:100 says 'the hit flash covers it', and speed_lines.gd:26-27 says 'the bots do' seed the rng, but only vfx_bot does;
- debug draw shows a blinking-in dummy's hurtboxes as live.

Smaller items noted without a verdict:
- WP4's 'lying poses close to M1's': every lying body, the limp KO included, lies spread-eagle and can't be told apart from a posed knockdown;
- the first-person spin kick: all three targets are below the view, so their flashes are never seen;
- the blood splash slides down a launched body;
- hit-04 fixer's edge case: another victim's flash inside a finisher's impact frame stays hidden;
- ragdoll_bot and combo_bot don't reseed VfxDirector's rng, so A/B pairs (--central-kick, --set, --tune) also differ in VFX;
- perf notes for Milestone 3: a blocked dummy re-runs _respawn_spot every tick (134-169 µs), sleeping ragdolls still run the modifier, vanished actors keep ticking, and bot exits print 'ERROR: resources still in use'.

gap_review_brief:
ROLE: gap reviewer for Milestone 2, phase 3, package C, round 2. You review only: change no tracked file. Work in /Users/arachne/repos/beat-em-up-PoC/.worktrees/m2-review-gap. It is detached at bba8633, its game code is identical to 8f5519f (the merged build: phase 3, round 1's 17 fixes and hit-04's fix), and it is already imported. cd there for every command. Everything you write, including probe bots (.gd and .tscn), goes under captures/review_gap/.

The machine is shared: run one Godot process at a time and never leave one running. Record with Movie Maker directly, NEVER with tools/capture_combos.sh:
`godot --path . --write-movie captures/review_gap/<name>.avi --fixed-fps 60 --resolution 1280x720 res://tests/bot/<bot>.tscn -- --act=<title text> > captures/review_gap/<name>.log 2>&1`
- --act takes a|b alternatives.
- ragdoll_bot also takes --central-kick and --set=<tunable>=<value>.
- combo_bot takes --tune=<prop>=<number>, but it forces dummy_health to 500.
- The movies come out at 1600x900, and video frame = physics frame - 1.

Tile stills with ffmpeg (`-vf "fps=12,scale=480:-1,tile=5x4" -frames:v 1`, or 30-60 per second around contacts) and LOOK at every sheet with the Read tool. Judge from frames, not code. Reuse the hit reviewer's helpers: copy white.sh, lum.sh, sheet.sh and fdiff.sh from /Users/arachne/repos/beat-em-up-PoC/.worktrees/m2-review-hit/captures/review_hit/. For probe bots, follow /Users/arachne/repos/beat-em-up-PoC/.worktrees/m2-review-grab/captures/review_grab/probe_bot.gd: extend res://tests/bot/combo_bot.gd and override _run with your own acts. The room:
- dummy posts at (-0.8,0,-1.8), (-0.5,0,0) and (-0.8,0,1.8); the player starts at (-4,0,0);
- building fronts face the street at z = -7;
- the near curb is 0.6 m high at z 7.0-7.5;
- crates at (-7,0.5,-4.5), (-6,0.5,-5.2) and (8,0.5,4.5).

ALREADY FOUND (cite by id, don't re-report):
- code-01 to -06, ragdoll-01 to -05, grab-01 to -08 (all fixed except grab-03 and grab-05);
- hit-01 (the flurry's strobe), hit-02 (a hit on the player in first person), hit-03 (the combat log in side view), hit-04 (fixed: a finisher's flash now shows on the 2 frames after its impact frame), hit-05 (side-view burst sizes, to fix);
- perf-01 (the first hit's material build), perf-02 (the damage-look shader variant).

APPROVED (not defects):
- heavy-tier knockdowns get the full ragdoll;
- staggers at 0.9 influence;
- KO bodies lie, blink off and vanish, and dummies blink back in at their post, or beside it if it is occupied, with no hits or grabs during the blink-in;
- KO bodies take no hits;
- the contact push with spin caps;
- the localized flash;
- the grab view pans down, with the lens moving back and up while holding;
- the knee rises a little to the right;
- the throw ends in the stance;
- the victim stands 6 cm closer;
- phase 1's eight defaults;
- the gray trousers and the dark hair.

OPEN WITH GAME-BOY (report what you see, propose no default change):
- more contortion on the contact push;
- the lens pull-back and the bend's depth;
- the combat log (grab-03, hit-03);
- the flash's first-person size and the flurry strobe (grab-05, hit-01);
- a hit on the player in first person (hit-02);
- a minimum size for the side-view flash;
- the hold's look dead band;
- bars over the middle of a body that isn't upright.

PART A, AFTER-CAPTURES NOBODY BUT THE FIXERS JUDGED (required)
1. Record every ragdoll_bot act in both views in one run (26 acts). Judge the first-person acts especially; on the merged build only the side views have been seen, and only for hit effects. Check:
   - **Hook stagger, both views:** ragdoll-02's fix added head and arm influence 0.45 and back share 0.5. Does it read in first person without flopping, and does it rock back from the side? Are the guard break, shove and parry staggers unchanged?
   - **Throw, both views:** launch-from-hold's arc plus hold-view's arm-out strike pose. Any pop or skate? Does anything come within 0.25 m of the lens or cover more than half the view?
   - **'Knee KOs the held dummy', both views.**
   - **KO cycle, both views:** the bar drains, then fades before the first blink-off; then the blink-off, the vanish, and the blink-in at the post.
   - **Stomp, both views:** does the foot land on top of the body? Are the player's standing feet inside the lying body's pelvis (the fixer's leftover)? Does the bar cross the player's shins?
   - **Push-kick pile:** does a lying body's bar cross the standing body?
2. hit-04 at close range. Record combo_bot 'P · P: jab, flurry (mash), shove|P P · P: jab, jab, spinning backfist|K · K|P P K|Hold P, release: haymaker|Pipe: pick up, 3 swings, throw' (all first person), plus ragdoll_bot 'flurry, finisher shove' (first person). For every finisher, find the 2 impact frames, then measure the white share (pixel luma 235 or more and 200 or more) on the 2 frames after them, and on 2 baseline frames. Give the shove after the flurry (about 0.4 m) in particular, with a sheet; compare hit-01's pre-fix numbers (12-13% and about 18%). Report data for Game-boy only.

PART B, EDGE CASES NOBODY PROBED (required; capture each in both views where useful)
1. **The player's own KO.** Set the player's health low in a probe and let a sparring jab KO it, in two cases:
   - (i) standing, in first person and side view;
   - (ii) while holding a dummy, with a second dummy jabbing the player.

   Judge:
   - Does the held body freeze in the hit's hitstop, then stagger away (grab-02's fix)?
   - Does the hold view ease out with no pop?
   - What does the first-person lens show on the KO? Is anything within 0.25 m, or covering more than half the view?
   - The player must not blink off, and auto_revive must bring it back after player_revive_s.
   - The log must have no SCRIPT ERROR or ERROR.
2. **Bodies against geometry.** Put a dummy with its back 0.3-0.5 m from the building front or a crate:
   - land the hook (contact push), the uppercut and the haymaker on it;
   - grab it there and knee it while pinned;
   - throw a held dummy into the wall from point-blank;
   - launch one onto or over the curb.

   Judge: limbs through geometry, jitter, explosion, NaN, a body stuck in the wall or the curb.
3. **The thrown pipe in side view.** Pick up, 3 swings, throw: the swings, the heavy-tier full-ragdoll knockdown, and where its burst and flash land after code-01's fix.
4. **Simultaneous KOs.** The spin kick on three dummies at max_health about 10, in both views: three KOs, blink-offs and respawns at once. Also a respawn beside an occupied post (the player standing on the post), on video. Does that dummy later walk back onto the occupied post (return_home)?

PART C, CODE READ OF THE FIX DIFFS (required, bounded; read and reason, no new recordings)
Read `git diff c27afaf 8f5519f -- game tools/gen_moves.gd` (about 1000 game lines in 13 files).
1. Check CLAUDE.md's rules:
   - simulation never reads a camera, and presentation writes no game state. Check EnemyHealthBars.screen_anchor_of(actor, camera), player._on_hit_received's TimeController.hitstop([_held]) and CombatActor.impact_frame_ticks;
   - no feel numbers in scripts;
   - static types;
   - ## docs on the new public API: hurt_point, show_flash, flash_at's shown parameter, is_blinking_in, get_hold_view_shift, get_hold_view_pitch_deg, Ragdoll.start's at_once, top_contact_twist, Tuning._migrate.
2. Check that the four new tunables are re-read on Tuning.changed: ragdoll_partial_head_influence, ragdoll_partial_arm_influence, ragdoll_stagger_back_share and grab_view_target_pitch_deg.
3. Check the interactions between fixes built on separate branches:
   - the delayed finisher flash against follow_flash and show_visual_pose, a KO launch, _vanish, reset_state and the parry's set_flash;
   - _launch's from_hold path against grab-02's release when the holder is hit on the same tick a knee lands, or the holder is KO'd;
   - _turn_solid and the ghost blink-in against magnetism, the pipe and other dummies' respawn queries;
   - a preset saved before the fixers' new tunables.
4. Rule on the code reviewer's leftover notes:
   - blink_shown()'s hard-coded 50% duty (combat_actor.gd:260);
   - _respawn_spot()'s rings [1, 2] times 2 body radii (training_dummy.gd:290-294);
   - return_home's 60 frames and 0.3 m;
   - humanoid_rig.gd:405's '3 m' against 4 m elsewhere;
   - the stale comments at vfx_bot.gd:100 and speed_lines.gd:26-27.

PART D (only if headroom remains)
- combo_bot 'Block: sparring jab from the front|Block: sparring jab (side view)': the side-view block spark at the view-share floor and the 0.45 guard flash.
- A current-build A/B of the contact push against the central kick (ragdoll_bot, with and without --central-kick) for the hook, the uppercut, the haymaker, the spinning heel and the guard break, in both views, for the open contortion question.
- A grab while a second dummy touches the victim.

RETURN:
- Findings, each with: id gap-NN, lens 'gap', title, severity, evidence (capture path and frame, log line, or diff file:line), repro, suggested fix, the files a fix touches, and spec_change.
- One verdict line each for A1's six checks, A2's finishers (with numbers), B1-B4, and C's four groups.
- The acts and probes checked, with their views.
- An explicit list of what you didn't get to.

Spec questions go to the lead and stay out of fixes.
